    {
      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "To find the number of positive divisors of a number, we can use the prime factorization method.\n\nFirst, we factorize the number $24$:\n$24 = 2^3 \\cdot 3^1$.\n\nThen, we use the formula for finding the number of divisors:\n\nIf a number $n$ has the prime factorization $n = 2^a \\cdot 3^b \\cdot 5^c \\cdot \\ldots$, the number of positive divisors of $n$ is given by $(a+1)(b+1)(c+1) \\cdots$.\n\nIn this case, $n = 24 = 2^3 \\cdot 3^1$, so the number of positive divisors of $24$ is $(3+1)(1+1) = \\boxed{8}$.",
